From d1c061caf2d6e69718b5fc47420a1a9eb29b9ee9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phil Elwell <phil@raspberrypi.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:34:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: Report non-HT 20MHz channels when HT is
 unsupported

brcmf_cfg80211_get_channel reports every 20MHz chanspec as
NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_20, i.e. HT20, even when the band has no HT
capabilities. That happens when the firmware's locale disables 11n
(nmode=0) - the SYN43436s CLM does this for RU, UA, BY and the world
locales, among others - because brcmf_setup_wiphybands then never
registers any HT capabilities.

cfg80211 rejects an HT20 chandef on a band without HT, so 60 seconds
after every regulatory hint reg_check_chans_work decides that the
station's channel is unusable and disconnects it (reason 3). The
reconnection brings another hint from the AP's Country IE, giving an
endless disconnect/reconnect cycle every ~61 seconds.

Report NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_20_NOHT when the band has no HT capabilities.

See: https://github.com/raspberrypi/firmware/issues/2019

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Phil Elwell <phil@raspberrypi.com>
---
 .../net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c  | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -5922,7 +5922,14 @@ static int brcmf_cfg80211_get_channel(st
 		width = NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_40;
 		break;
 	case BRCMU_CHAN_BW_20:
-		width = NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_20;
+		/* cfg80211 rejects an HT20 chandef if the band has no HT
+		 * capabilities, which happens when the firmware's locale
+		 * disables 11n (nmode=0).
+		 */
+		if (wiphy->bands[band] && wiphy->bands[band]->ht_cap.ht_supported)
+			width = NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_20;
+		else
+			width = NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_20_NOHT;
 		break;
 	case BRCMU_CHAN_BW_80P80:
 		width = NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_80P80;
